{
  "index_test": "whole-animal-in-vivo",
  "index_test_evidence": "In this study, we collected retrospective information from 598 animals (509 WT/GA mice, 89 WT/GA rats): 336 animals subjected to treatment (MASLD-inducing conditions: 315 animals; or CCl 4 : 21 animals) and 262 animals as controls for MASLD-inducing conditions (247 animals) or CCl 4 (15 animals), returning 39 models (that is, study designs) aimed at modeling MASLD, and two time points for CCl 4 (positive controls of MASLD-independent fibrosis).",
  "decision": "include",
  "reason": "The study uses whole-animal in vivo models (mice and rats) to predict human clinical outcomes (MASLD). It quantifies the agreement between animal models and human disease through a 'human proximity score' (MHPS) based on metabolic phenotype, liver histology, and liver transcriptome data. This directly addresses the criteria for inclusion."
}
